1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,439
Terror From the Grave: no single Killer, just the dead, rising in endless numbers.

2
00:00:04,659 --> 00:00:06,344
Here's how this vignette plays.

3
00:00:07,167 --> 00:00:11,494
There's no Killer board: line up the two Bloodlust cards instead, with the marker on

4
00:00:11,494 --> 00:00:13,503
the start space. Horror starts at four.

5
00:00:13,723 --> 00:00:18,069
No Killer is placed. Put one Zombie on each exit and on the Killer's start space.

6
00:00:18,069 --> 00:00:22,576
With only one exit, put one there, two on the start space and one on a search space.

7
00:00:22,796 --> 00:00:27,268
Put a Horde token on the face-down Dark Power card, and shuffle the four Vehicle

8
00:00:27,268 --> 00:00:30,007
tokens face down, spread evenly across the exits.

9
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:32,927
To win, kill every Zombie and every Horde.

10
00:00:32,927 --> 00:00:35,271
The moment none are left on the board, you win.

11
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:39,422
You lose immediately if three Hordes are in play and a fourth would be created, or

12
00:00:39,422 --> 00:00:39,949
if you die.

13
00:00:40,767 --> 00:00:43,071
Zombies are tokens, and count as Minions.

14
00:00:43,291 --> 00:00:47,330
When you see the spawn icon, spawn the number of Zombies shown at the current

15
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:51,578
Bloodlust level. Place them one at a time on exit spaces, always the one with the

16
00:00:51,578 --> 00:00:54,725
fewest Zombies first. Ties go to the exit farthest from you.

17
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:59,714
Zombies are slow. They move only once per Killer phase, during the Minion Action,

18
00:00:59,714 --> 00:01:01,933
and ignore every move icon on Terror cards.

19
00:01:02,153 --> 00:01:06,342
They use the normal targeting rules, except that a Zombie that can't reach its

20
00:01:06,342 --> 00:01:09,940
target panics instead: it shambles one space in a random direction.

21
00:01:10,767 --> 00:01:14,850
Zombies in a space attack together, at one target, dealing damage equal to the

22
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:18,148
number of Zombies there. They always go for Victims before you.

23
00:01:18,368 --> 00:01:23,069
Every Victim killed by Zombies is replaced with a Zombie token, and Bloodlust rises

24
00:01:23,069 --> 00:01:24,939
as normal. Losses feed the swarm.

25
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:29,871
At the end of the Killer phase, any space with three or more Zombies becomes a

26
00:01:29,871 --> 00:01:34,081
Horde. Replace them with a Horde token; the first one uses the token on the Dark

27
00:01:34,081 --> 00:01:36,028
Power card, revealing the Dark Power.

28
00:01:36,248 --> 00:01:40,063
A Horde's health equals the number of Zombies that formed it, at least three,

29
00:01:40,063 --> 00:01:43,629
tracked on a Victim Holding board. Hordes don't use Final Health tokens.

30
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:48,930
A Horde counts as a Killer: Victims won't follow you into its space, and it uses the

31
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:51,606
Movement and Attack values on the Bloodlust track.

32
00:01:51,606 --> 00:01:56,103
If a card moves or places the Killer, use only the Horde closest to the destination.

33
00:01:56,323 --> 00:02:00,568
Each Victim it kills adds a health. It has no maximum, and gains a health from any

34
00:02:00,568 --> 00:02:04,813
heal effect. If it shares a space with a Zombie, it absorbs it for another health.

35
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:09,567
A Horde never breaks back into Zombies, even below three health, and two Hordes in a

36
00:02:09,567 --> 00:02:13,993
space don't combine. Effects that kill X Zombies deal X damage to a Horde instead.

37
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:18,944
Each location has one special vehicle with its own Vehicle Action card.

38
00:02:18,944 --> 00:02:21,454
Ignore that location's normal vehicle Item;

39
00:02:21,454 --> 00:02:24,315
if it turns up, swap it for a random unused Item.

40
00:02:24,535 --> 00:02:27,691
The first time you enter an exit, reveal its Vehicle tokens.

41
00:02:27,691 --> 00:02:31,953
If you find the vehicle, remove all the tokens, put the vehicle in your space, or

42
00:02:31,953 --> 00:02:35,109
the nearest water space for boats, and take its Action card.

43
00:02:35,109 --> 00:02:36,951
It then works like any Action card.

44
00:02:37,171 --> 00:02:40,689
If the card's title has the driver icon, you can use it from anywhere.

45
00:02:40,689 --> 00:02:44,509
Otherwise you must be with the vehicle, and normal moves can bring it along.

46
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:49,464
The Dark Powers. Runners: Zombies now follow move icons, always moving before

47
00:02:49,464 --> 00:02:53,435
attacks. Legion: every spawn adds one more Zombie at the exit nearest you.

48
00:02:53,435 --> 00:02:57,673
Super Horde: Hordes that meet merge, and any Horde with twelve health makes you

49
00:02:57,673 --> 00:02:57,941
lose.

50
00:02:58,161 --> 00:03:01,490
In every Finale, all Zombies and Hordes move before any attacks.

51
00:03:01,490 --> 00:03:05,755
Their Numbers Are Endless costs you a health whenever no Enemy is in your space at

52
00:03:05,755 --> 00:03:10,020
the end of your Action phase. They've All Been Bitten turns every remaining Victim

53
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:10,748
into a Zombie.

54
00:03:11,567 --> 00:03:15,450
A few tips. Break up groups of Zombies before the end of the Killer phase, so they

55
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:16,303
can't form Hordes.

56
00:03:16,523 --> 00:03:20,213
Keep Victims away from them: every one they kill becomes another Zombie.

57
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:23,469
And hunt for the vehicle early; it's often your best weapon.

58
00:03:23,469 --> 00:03:23,975
Good luck.

